1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:04,331
When you were five, one summer lasted forever.

2
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,053
Now a whole year slips by between two birthdays.

3
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:20,148
Here's one idea. At five, a year is a fifth of your whole life.

4
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,904
At fifty, it's one fiftieth. Each year is a smaller slice.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,663
But there's a stranger reason.

6
00:00:28,713 --> 00:00:31,950
Your brain doesn't keep a clock. It keeps memories.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,137
A first day at school. The first time you saw the sea.

8
00:00:35,187 --> 00:00:37,144
New things leave marks.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,655
Routine leaves almost none. A hundred mornings fold into one.

10
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:46,181
So looking back, a year without new memories feels short.

11
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,517
The fix? Do something new. Go somewhere. Learn something.

12
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,515
Fill the page, and the year gets longer again.
